       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Higher doses raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little extra blood pressure control.\n\nPlease tell me which of these you want:\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, a typical starting dose. You could titrate up to 10 mg if needed.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written**, if the dose is intentional. I'd add a note giving the rationale, and you may want to confirm it with pharmacy.\n\nIf the target is better BP control and 10 mg isn't enough, adding a second agent such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide is usually preferred over going above 10 mg."
      }
